# PR ship and agent review (contract)

When the user asks to **ship**, **submit**, **open a PR**, or **babysit agent review**, work in a **stack worktree** only (see `.cursor/rules/pr-workflow.mdc`).

**Read** [`.cursor/skills/ship-and-review/SKILL.md`](../skills/ship-and-review/SKILL.md) before the agent-review loop — full CI loop, triage, quota, CodeRabbit, Bugbot, and exit-code detail live there. **`scripts/wait-for-agent-review --help`** is the exit-code SSOT.

Helper scripts:

- **`scripts/wait-for-agent-review`** — poll, triage, email (no self-approve)
- **`scripts/trigger-agent-review`** — request a review from the configured agent

Configure `~/.config/agent-review.env` from `etc/agent-review.env.example` (`AGENT_REVIEW_REPORT_TO`, SMTP).

## Happy path

Prefer the all-in-one (runs pre-pr-checks, submit, CI wait, then the agent-review loop):

```bash
scripts/dev/ship-and-review
```

Or the manual phases (mutually exclusive with `ship-and-review` above — do not chain both):

```bash
scripts/dev/pre-pr-checks
scripts/dev/submit-stack                       # includes post-pr-submission-checks
./scripts/wait-for-agent-review loop --pr <n>  # when CI is green
```

After every later push, re-run **`scripts/dev/post-pr-submission-checks --pr <n>`** before agent review or merge. Do not skip CI wait unless the user opts out.

## Agent review essentials

> **Reply before resolve (required):** Post an on-thread human reply via **`reply-thread`** (or `reply-comment`) **before** **`resolve-thread`**. Exit **3** means threads lack a human reply. Pending feedback also includes operator-authored PR conversation comments until an explicit URL-citing reply + **`resolve-comment`**.

When `check` reports **`complete_ready: true`** (requires **agent sign-off** on the current head — not a bare CodeRabbit status):

```bash
./scripts/wait-for-agent-review complete --pr <n>
```

- **No self-approve** — `complete` emails the operator; it does not run `gh pr review --approve`.
- **No `merge-it`** unless the user explicitly asked.

## Exit codes (condensed)

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Success / `complete_ready` / PR merged |
| 1 | Usage or prerequisite error |
| 2 | Wait: not fresh yet, pending CI, or transient mergeability |
| 3 | Threads lack a human reply (triage; use `reply-thread`) |
| 4 | `BEHIND` — run `wait-for-agent-review restack` |
| 5 | Fresh review but agent not empty yet |
| 6 | PR non-convergence timeout (12h cap) — give-up |
| 7 | All agent quotas exhausted — give-up |
| 8 | Agent GitHub check failed to run |
| 9 | Wait idle break (`loop` continues) |
| 10 | Required CI failed — agent fixes and resumes (no email; escalate only if unfixable) |
| 11 | Permanent merge block — human intervention |

See the Skill for triage of issue comments and pull-request review bodies, CodeRabbit on_push (`@coderabbitai review` is forbidden), cooldown/full-review gate, quota fallback chain, and give-up/complete paths.
